1
00:00:17,410 --> 00:00:20,490
We welcome you to the magician's guild.

2
00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:24,040
Could you please show me the usual list?

3
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:26,750
As you wish, Lord Sebas.

4
00:00:39,510 --> 00:00:45,140
Would you tell me a little more
about this "Floating Board" spell?

5
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:52,230
Yes. Floating Board is a first tier spell
that creates a floating translucent board.

6
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:54,650
The spell is essentially used
for transporting items,

7
00:00:54,650 --> 00:00:56,660
and employed in public works projects.

8
00:00:56,660 --> 00:00:58,160
I see.

9
00:00:58,490 --> 00:01:03,250
Then I will purchase one such magic scroll.

10
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:08,170
Thank you very much. That will be
one gold and ten silver coins, please.

11
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:26,140
Shadow Demon, please tell Solution for me

12
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:30,480
that I am looking around the city,
so I will be a little late.

13
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:33,240
Now then...

14
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:37,200
I think I will head over there today.

15
00:01:58,630 --> 00:02:01,390
Shadow Demon, go!

16
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:31,660
Would you please remove your hand?

17
00:04:04,390 --> 00:04:06,850
Are you in some need of assistance?

18
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:09,200
If that is the case...

19
00:04:11,890 --> 00:04:15,330
Hey, old guy, where the hell
did you blow in from?

20
00:04:19,650 --> 00:04:20,670
Eh?

21
00:04:22,950 --> 00:04:25,490
Let me go, you old geezer!

22
00:04:25,990 --> 00:04:28,330
What is this woman?

23
00:04:28,330 --> 00:04:31,080
O-One of our employees!

24
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:36,460
So you did this to her with full knowledge
that she is human, did you?

25
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:41,570
And what are you going to do with her now?

26
00:04:42,550 --> 00:04:45,220
Take her to the temple, because she's sick...

27
00:04:48,390 --> 00:04:52,220
Then you will not have a problem
if I take her away.

28
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:55,600
L-Legally speaking, she belongs to us!

29
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:58,650
If you take her away, it would be kidnapping!

30
00:04:58,650 --> 00:05:01,150
Should a proper butler
be getting himself mixed up in trouble

31
00:05:01,150 --> 00:05:03,900
behind his master's back?

32
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:05,900
Fair enough.

33
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:09,990
Do you want me to help you?

34
00:05:12,410 --> 00:05:14,500
Do you want me to help you?

35
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,630
I am not inclined to help a person at my feet

36
00:05:25,630 --> 00:05:27,790
who can only pray for salvation to come,

37
00:05:27,790 --> 00:05:32,770
like a plant, showered upon
by the rains falling from the heavens.

38
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:36,770
However, if you are someone
struggling to live...

39
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:41,260
...forget about the terror, and go to sleep.

40
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:45,650
You are now under my protection.

41
00:05:45,650 --> 00:05:48,030
Like hell! I never agreed to this, did I?!

42
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:50,750
Like hell, you say?

43
00:05:51,490 --> 00:05:56,080
Are you trying to say that what I said
to the likes of you was false?

44
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:57,940
Uh, no...

45
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:02,040
Then I will take her with me.

46
00:06:04,130 --> 00:06:05,760
W-Wait!

47
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:07,590
Is there something else?

48
00:06:07,590 --> 00:06:08,510
No!

49
00:06:08,510 --> 00:06:12,140
If you take her with you,
it will spell trouble for me!

50
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:15,720
L-Look, you must know about them, right?

51
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,470
Eight Fingers?

52
00:06:20,230 --> 00:06:23,250
The ones who control the kingdom
behind the scenes?

53
00:06:24,230 --> 00:06:28,860
So, you get it? I'm begging you,
pretend you didn't see anything!

54
00:06:31,530 --> 00:06:33,490
I am taking her with me.

55
00:06:33,490 --> 00:06:37,260
Come on, have a heart! I'll be killed!

56
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:42,540
Saving someone who is in trouble
is common sense!

57
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:49,130
Platinum coins?! Wh-What are these for?

58
00:06:49,130 --> 00:06:52,430
Take that money and
hire an adventurer or whatever.

59
00:06:52,430 --> 00:06:56,250
That should be more than enough
to allow you to flee the country.

60
00:06:56,930 --> 00:07:01,950
If you run as fast as you can,
it should buy you a little bit of time.

61
00:07:03,270 --> 00:07:05,400
Welcome back, Lord Seba--

62
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:08,400
Lord Sebas, what is <i>that</i>?

63
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:10,350
I found her.

64
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:15,280
I see. I doubt that
you meant it as a gift for me.

65
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:17,190
What are you going to do with it?

66
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:22,290
What indeed? Will you begin
by healing her wounds for me?

67
00:07:22,290 --> 00:07:24,790
Wounds... you say?

68
00:07:24,790 --> 00:07:28,260
Could you have not left that
at the temple, then?

69
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:33,040
I <i>could</i> have. Imagine, <i>me</i>, of all people,
not realizing such a thing.

70
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,720
Shall I go dispose of it now?

71
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:39,060
No. I have already brought her this far.

72
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:43,100
We should think of some effective use for her.

73
00:07:45,770 --> 00:07:50,280
Can I ask you to start
by assessing her physical condition?

74
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:53,340
Very well. Right away.

75
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:03,080
I will let you take it from here.

76
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:04,480
Very well.

77
00:08:08,710 --> 00:08:10,800
What foolish conduct.

78
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:14,890
"Saving someone who is in trouble
is common sense."

79
00:08:14,890 --> 00:08:20,810
That is what the Supreme One who created me,
Lord Touch Me, always said.

80
00:08:21,270 --> 00:08:25,810
Could that be the reason why
<i>I</i> do the same, as well?

81
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:29,070
Might it actually be a curse?

82
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:36,740
How did it go?

83
00:08:37,950 --> 00:08:41,040
Syphilis and two other venereal diseases.

84
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:43,870
Several cracked ribs, as well as fingers.

85
00:08:43,870 --> 00:08:46,750
The tendons in the right arm
and left leg have been torn.

86
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:49,500
Upper and lower front teeth have been pulled.

87
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:51,380
There is also an anal fissure.

88
00:08:51,380 --> 00:08:55,260
There is a possibility that the woman
is addicted to some kind of drug.

89
00:08:55,260 --> 00:08:57,510
In addition, there are
multiple bruises and lacerations--

90
00:08:57,510 --> 00:08:59,010
Can she be treated?

91
00:08:59,010 --> 00:09:00,180
Easily.

92
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:01,560
Then please see to it.

93
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:04,180
Would it not be better to call in Lady Pestonya,

94
00:09:04,180 --> 00:09:06,530
and have her use healing magic?

95
00:09:06,530 --> 00:09:11,570
Solution, you are in possession
of healing scrolls, aren't you?

96
00:09:11,570 --> 00:09:13,530
Please use one of those.

97
00:09:13,530 --> 00:09:19,330
Lord Sebas, the scrolls were
granted to us by the Supreme Ones.

98
00:09:19,330 --> 00:09:23,040
I humbly submit that they are
not to be used on the likes of humans.

99
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:24,410
Do it.

100
00:09:24,410 --> 00:09:29,540
As you wish. Will rendering
the woman uninjured--or rather,

101
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:32,000
restoration of the woman's physical state

102
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:36,130
before engaging in
those activities be sufficient?

103
00:09:36,130 --> 00:09:37,590
Once her treatment is complete,

104
00:09:37,590 --> 00:09:41,390
can I ask you to draw her a bath
and clean her up?

105
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:44,560
I will go buy something for supper.

106
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:48,020
Lord Sebas, if you wish
to tend to her mental state,

107
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:51,570
I think it best that we call on Lord Ains.

108
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:56,320
This is not something into which
we need to bring Lord Ains.

109
00:10:01,330 --> 00:10:05,910
I would have understood if Sebas
had agreed to let you be my plaything

110
00:10:05,910 --> 00:10:09,110
once you were fully recovered...

111
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:12,540
Perhaps I will devour you first...

112
00:10:14,050 --> 00:10:16,860
...before Lord Sebas returns.

113
00:10:25,680 --> 00:10:29,900
I believe you have been completely healed.
How are you feeling?

114
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:34,540
Are you hungry?
I brought you something to eat.

115
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:36,800
Go ahead.

116
00:11:07,730 --> 00:11:10,770
As long as you are here,
you are not in any kind of danger.

117
00:11:10,770 --> 00:11:13,020
You have my guarantee.

118
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:16,780
When you wake up, you will still be in this bed.

119
00:11:19,070 --> 00:11:25,810
Th-Thank... you... very... much...

120
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:32,960
Think nothing of it.
Now that I have taken you in,

121
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:36,320
I will ensure your safety
to the best of my ability.

122
00:11:41,130 --> 00:11:45,100
Why... didn't... anyone...

123
00:11:50,230 --> 00:11:53,560
...help... me... any... sooner...?

124
00:11:56,770 --> 00:11:58,820
You're all right now.

125
00:12:01,990 --> 00:12:03,820
You're all right now.

126
00:12:17,090 --> 00:12:20,130
I-I'm... sorry...

127
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,710
Please don't concern yourself.

128
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:28,430
For a man, it is an honor to offer
his breast for a woman to lean on.

129
00:12:32,230 --> 00:12:39,610
But... I couldn't...
accept... such a... clean...

130
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:49,090
Here. Take it.

131
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:53,170
A handkerchief that goes unused
is a thing to be mourned.

132
00:12:53,540 --> 00:12:57,750
Especially a handkerchief
that is not allowed to dry one's tears.

133
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:05,010
Please, get some rest. When you get up,
we will discuss what comes next.

134
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:09,430
What... comes next...?

135
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:12,980
You are probably uneasy
about remaining in the capital.

136
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:15,190
Is there anywhere else that you can go?

137
00:13:16,690 --> 00:13:18,200
I see.

138
00:13:20,110 --> 00:13:21,770
Well then, let's see...

139
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:25,270
Would you mind telling me your name?

140
00:13:26,570 --> 00:13:32,790
I-I am... T-Tuare...

141
00:13:32,790 --> 00:13:34,290
Tuare, you say?

142
00:13:35,210 --> 00:13:38,670
Oh, yes, I have not yet
told you my name, have I?

143
00:13:38,670 --> 00:13:42,170
My name is Sebas Tian.

144
00:13:42,710 --> 00:13:45,420
Please feel free to call me Sebas.

145
00:13:50,010 --> 00:13:51,110
Okay...

146
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:58,520
Hmm? Is something the matter?

147
00:13:59,270 --> 00:14:00,310
Lord Sebas,

148
00:14:00,310 --> 00:14:03,240
what are you planning
to end up doing with that woman?

149
00:14:05,650 --> 00:14:07,910
You are talking about Tuare, right?

150
00:14:07,910 --> 00:14:08,820
A name...?

151
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:14,330
Lord Sebas, I do not know what reasons
you had for taking that woman in,

152
00:14:14,790 --> 00:14:19,330
but one receives those kinds of injuries
by being in a certain environment.

153
00:14:19,330 --> 00:14:21,590
Will not those who those who did those things

154
00:14:21,590 --> 00:14:25,300
be displeased that the woman is still alive?

155
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:28,180
If any problems do arise,

156
00:14:28,180 --> 00:14:30,340
I will take measures to deal with them.

157
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:34,100
I would like you to wait
and see what happens for a little while.

158
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:37,100
You can do that, right, Solution?

159
00:14:40,730 --> 00:14:44,140
My speed of god blade attack, God Flash.

160
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:47,950
And my absolute area of perception, Field.

161
00:14:48,490 --> 00:14:51,120
If I combine these two attacks...

162
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:53,870
Blade Technique, Whistling Wind!

163
00:14:56,250 --> 00:14:58,790
M-Monster...

164
00:15:05,210 --> 00:15:08,510
Oh? Did you get tired?

165
00:15:08,510 --> 00:15:13,430
I must say, your nail clipper
sure is dull, isn't it?

166
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:34,310
Where am I...?

167
00:15:38,370 --> 00:15:39,850
You look terrible.

168
00:15:44,420 --> 00:15:46,980
Gazef... Stronoff?

169
00:15:51,470 --> 00:15:55,210
It was the championships of
the royal matches where we first met, right?

170
00:15:55,850 --> 00:16:00,230
I barely managed to win, but from the time
I took up the sword to this day,

171
00:16:00,230 --> 00:16:02,010
I've never had as close a battle as that.

172
00:16:09,990 --> 00:16:11,490
Unglaus?

173
00:16:14,530 --> 00:16:17,370
Brain Unglaus?

174
00:16:17,370 --> 00:16:21,300
Gazef... Stronoff...

175
00:16:23,210 --> 00:16:26,340
Unglaus, what the hell happened?

176
00:16:27,210 --> 00:16:31,090
Tell me, are we strong?

177
00:16:33,180 --> 00:16:37,820
Stronoff, we're weak. We're <i>weak</i>.

178
00:16:38,430 --> 00:16:41,770
Our skill with the sword
is no better than trash.

179
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:45,770
We're nothing more
than humans--an inferior race.

180
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:51,040
I don't understand you.
Any warrior knows that, don't they?

181
00:16:51,610 --> 00:16:54,150
Compared to ogres and giants, what are we?

182
00:16:54,570 --> 00:16:59,240
There are heights to be reached.
That's why we make the effort, isn't it?

183
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:04,120
No! That's not the level I mean, Stronoff!

184
00:17:04,120 --> 00:17:07,420
The real heights can't be reached,
no matter what kind of efforts we make!

185
00:17:08,210 --> 00:17:13,420
The human race can never reach them.
That's the truth about those heights!

186
00:17:14,090 --> 00:17:16,100
You saw something that extreme?

187
00:17:17,010 --> 00:17:22,270
I did. I experienced it.
A summit that humans can never arrive at.

188
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:25,810
No, what I saw wasn't even a height.

189
00:17:26,190 --> 00:17:28,770
I was so utterly lacking in ability,

190
00:17:29,230 --> 00:17:30,770
it was just a game.

191
00:17:31,230 --> 00:17:32,890
A farce.

192
00:17:34,530 --> 00:17:35,900
Stronoff,

193
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:39,410
the strength we gain
from the sword is worthless.

194
00:17:39,410 --> 00:17:41,660
In the face of true strength, it's rubbish.

195
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:46,680
I'm glad I got to see you one last time.

196
00:17:47,370 --> 00:17:48,880
Now I can die.

197
00:17:49,750 --> 00:17:51,130
Brain Unglaus!

198
00:17:53,840 --> 00:17:54,630
Sit down,

199
00:17:55,090 --> 00:17:56,540
and eat something!

200
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:59,430
Everything else comes afterward.

201
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:22,330
Everything is ready here.

202
00:18:22,330 --> 00:18:23,620
Flawless.

203
00:18:23,620 --> 00:18:28,500
Yeah, I know; I saw you.
I'm moving on to the next location.

204
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:32,210
I have to catch as big
a bigshot as possible, after all.

205
00:18:32,210 --> 00:18:35,960
We should move to attack now, as well.
What about the other two?

206
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:38,840
Probably goofing around,
since they aren't on for this.

207
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:40,680
The hell they aren't.

208
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:43,970
They're lying in wait near the village,
in case of emergency.

209
00:18:43,970 --> 00:18:47,810
Now, I'm off.
You two continue according to plan.

210
00:18:57,650 --> 00:19:00,730
This won't do anything more
than buy us some time.

211
00:19:01,660 --> 00:19:04,540
If we can't strike a blow somewhere
to turn things around,

212
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:05,840
then this is all futile.

213
00:19:12,710 --> 00:19:15,340
Yeah, it's burning quite nicely.

214
00:19:15,340 --> 00:19:18,330
I just hope the people
of the village can get away.

215
00:19:19,170 --> 00:19:23,760
We're burning the plant that
the diabolical drug Black Dust is made from.

216
00:19:23,760 --> 00:19:27,430
It's not just the fire; the smoke
would be bad to get caught in, too.

217
00:19:27,810 --> 00:19:30,730
So, we're going to go burn
someplace other than this, right?

218
00:19:30,730 --> 00:19:33,510
Yes, of course. We have to strike where we can.

219
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:36,650
Whatever else we do,
we have to prevent Black Dust

220
00:19:36,650 --> 00:19:38,720
from spreading like this across the kingdom.

221
00:19:39,610 --> 00:19:42,240
There are many other outposts besides this one

222
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:44,830
where they are cultivating drugs.

223
00:19:44,830 --> 00:19:48,000
Eight Fingers really is a huge organization.

224
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:52,250
It sure is, Gagaran.
The largest of the underworld syndicates.

225
00:19:52,250 --> 00:19:54,350
Big enough to undermine a whole nation.

226
00:19:56,050 --> 00:19:59,210
We finished as planned, fiendish leader.

227
00:19:59,210 --> 00:20:01,760
We left no evidence behind, fiendish boss.

228
00:20:04,220 --> 00:20:06,970
Tia and Tina, did you find anything?

229
00:20:06,970 --> 00:20:08,100
Nothing here.

230
00:20:08,100 --> 00:20:10,060
There was no valuable information.

231
00:20:10,060 --> 00:20:12,940
Ugh, so we hope for the best from Evileye.

232
00:20:14,230 --> 00:20:15,190
I've returned.

233
00:20:15,190 --> 00:20:17,360
Welcome back, Evileye.

234
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:19,110
Yeah. Hey, Lakyus,

235
00:20:19,110 --> 00:20:20,190
catch.

236
00:20:20,940 --> 00:20:22,070
What's this?

237
00:20:22,070 --> 00:20:23,200
A code?

238
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:24,950
Probably.

239
00:20:24,950 --> 00:20:27,830
This could be a lead on Eight Fingers.

240
00:20:32,290 --> 00:20:34,210
Let's now begin the meeting.

241
00:20:34,830 --> 00:20:36,500
There are several items on the agenda,

242
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:39,960
but the first thing we should
take care of is... Hilma?

243
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:41,440
Right, then.

244
00:20:43,430 --> 00:20:45,090
Word is that one of your drug-growing facilities

245
00:20:45,090 --> 00:20:48,510
has come under attack
by some unidentified assailants.

246
00:20:48,510 --> 00:20:51,600
Yes, it has. We were attacked.

247
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:54,480
It was a village where
we had a production facility.

248
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:56,270
Hell of an expenditure.

249
00:20:56,270 --> 00:20:59,900
It could put a bit of a squeeze
on our distribution.

250
00:20:59,900 --> 00:21:02,490
And you have no information on who they are?

251
00:21:02,490 --> 00:21:05,420
No, I don't. They were flawless.

252
00:21:05,990 --> 00:21:09,580
Which is why it's not impossible
to imagine who they might be.

253
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,370
Hmm.

254
00:21:11,370 --> 00:21:12,330
Hey...

255
00:21:12,330 --> 00:21:14,270
...don't you want to bring us in?

256
00:21:15,080 --> 00:21:18,590
You can't protect much with
that bunch of nobodies you put together.

257
00:21:18,590 --> 00:21:24,090
No thanks. I can't afford to let you guys
know about my strategic sites.

258
00:21:25,130 --> 00:21:29,100
In that case,
I'd like to take you up on that offer.

259
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:31,140
What's that, Cocco Doll?

260
00:21:31,140 --> 00:21:33,100
Can you afford to pay us,
when you're on the way out?

261
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:36,900
Don't worry, Zero. The slave trade
may be legally prohibited now,

262
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:41,860
thanks to the Golden Princess,
but I have plenty of funds.

263
00:21:41,860 --> 00:21:46,360
Ho, so you have something
that major going on, do you? Fine.

264
00:21:46,360 --> 00:21:49,740
Oh, thank you so.
I've had a bit of a problem come up

265
00:21:49,740 --> 00:21:52,160
with a woman who was
scheduled to be disposed of.

266
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:56,040
I think this will require me
to ready an excessive amount of force.

267
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:59,460
I can't very well have
that place of business going under.

268
00:21:59,460 --> 00:22:03,960
Rest assured, you can count on my men.
Those of us in Six Arms

269
00:22:04,380 --> 00:22:07,330
guarantee the safety of your property.

270
00:22:07,330 --> 00:22:09,330


